claimed: deploy-bootstrap-spec -- operator ask 2026-09-07: a clean machine must be handled properly -- install what can be installed, or at least TELL the operator plainly, never fail with a cryptic error and never fail silently. Spec section in specs/deployment.md: the Tool/Presence/Report model (missing, too old, and the state that actually happens most -- installed but not usable: a docker daemon that is down, a kubectl with no context, a flyctl that is not logged in), the report's shape and its exact per-platform install command, installation as an OPT-IN that prints the command before running it and never pipes a script from the internet into a shell, the rule that every shelled-out failure is wrapped with its command, exit code and last output, and Up refusing on the report rather than letting a missing binary fail somewhere inside. Spec only.
